# Kapuletu Admin Panel — Implementation Plan

## Audit Summary

- **Backend admin APIs** are fully implemented across 6 service files in `services/admin/`.
- **Notifications broadcast** lives in `services/notifications/router.py` under `POST /notifications/broadcast` — admin-only, already guarded by `get_admin_user`. It supports `in_app`, `email`, and `whatsapp` channels and three targeting modes (`all_members`, `specific_member`, `custom_selection`). This is **not** under the `/admin` prefix — it's its own service.
- **Frontend notifications page** at `/notifications` exists for user-facing display but has no admin-side management UI.
- **No new codebase.** All admin work is in the existing `kapuletu-frontend` Next.js app, extending `src/app/(protected)/admin/`.
- **Charting:** `recharts` is already installed.
- **Design tokens:** Figtree, `--primary: #097255`, `--color-burnt-amber: #EC7B23`, `--color-refined-blue: #1B4580`, existing shadcn/ui components.

---

## Design

- The admin panel **inherits the existing design system exactly** — same font (Figtree), same CSS tokens, same shadcn/ui components, same `IconLibrary`, same `StatCard`, `PageLayout`, `Table`, `Card`, `Badge`, `Dialog`, `Sheet`, `Tabs`.
- **No new typographies.** No new color palettes introduced.
- **Distinction from the treasurer workspace** comes from:
  - A denser sidebar with 9 nav items across 3 labeled sections
  - Header role badge continues to read **"Admin Workspace"** (existing code, no change)
  - All pages are data-dense: stat rows, tables, and action drawers

> [!IMPORTANT]
> No AI marketing language, no unnecessary verbosity. All UI copy is short, direct, and functional — consistent with the existing workspace tone.

---

## Access

- Admins and super admins use the **same login page** (`/login`).
- After login, the `user_role` cookie determines the workspace. `admin` and `super_admin` roles are routed to `/admin`.
- All roles (`admin`, `super_admin`) have the same capabilities in this phase. All write actions are attributed to the logged-in user via `current_user` in the backend.
- Destructive or irreversible actions require a **confirmation dialog** before the API call fires.

---

## Skeleton-First Approach

Phase 0 is the shell: layout, sidebar, topbar, routing, breadcrumbs, and stub pages. No module data is wired until the shell is approved and working.

**Skeleton deliverables:**
- Admin sidebar with all 9 nav items, section labels, icons, and active state
- Admin topbar: existing greeting, search, help, notifications, profile — no changes needed
- All `/admin/*` routes resolving without 404
- Breadcrumb labels extended for all new routes
- Module pages exist as stubs (skeleton loaders or `ComingSoon`)

