- **Payments** — paginated table (User, Amount KES, Status badge, Date), filterable by status
- **Override** — form to manually apply a plan to a user (user_id, plan_id, duration)

**New components:** `AdminFinancePage`, `PlanCard`, `CreatePlanSheet`, `PaymentsTable`, `ManualOverrideForm`

---

### Module 5 — Notifications (`/admin/notifications`)
**APIs:** `POST /notifications/broadcast`, `GET /notifications` (read-only platform view)

This is the admin-side management of the notifications system.

- **Broadcast tab** — compose a notification: title, message, channel selection (`in_app`, `email`, `whatsapp`), target type (`all_members`, `specific_member`, `custom_selection`). If specific/custom: user ID input. Recipient count preview. Send behind confirmation dialog.
- **History tab** — read-only log of recent broadcasts sent (title, channels, target, timestamp). Sourced from audit logs or a future broadcast log endpoint.

> [!NOTE]
> `POST /notifications/broadcast` is already admin-gated (`get_admin_user`). The frontend just needs to call it.

**New components:** `AdminNotificationsPage`, `BroadcastForm`, `BroadcastConfirmDialog`, `BroadcastHistoryTable`

---

### Module 6 — Support Tickets (`/admin/support`)
**APIs:** `GET /admin/crm/tickets`, `PATCH /admin/crm/tickets/{id}`

- Table: Subject, Category, Priority (`Badge`), Status, Created, Assigned
- Filter: status (open / in-progress / resolved)
- Row click → `Sheet`: full ticket view, status dropdown, internal notes textarea, resolve/assign button

**New components:** `AdminSupportPage`, `TicketsTable`, `TicketDetailSheet`

---

### Module 7 — Broadcast (`/admin/broadcast`)
**APIs:** `POST /admin/crm/broadcast` (SMS broadcast via SQS), `POST /notifications/broadcast` (in-app / email / whatsapp)

- Two broadcast methods on separate tabs:
  - **Platform Notification** — uses `/notifications/broadcast` (in-app, email, whatsapp)
  - **SMS Broadcast** — uses `/admin/crm/broadcast` (SQS → Twilio)
- Message compose area, channel/method selection, confirmation dialog showing estimated recipient count before send

> [!NOTE]
> Broadcast (the outbound communication action) is a separate module from Support Tickets (inbound user issues). These are now distinct sidebar items.

**New components:** `AdminBroadcastPage`, `NotificationBroadcastTab`, `SMSBroadcastTab`

---

